[2026-01-30T08:07:21.318Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017193d1CHZWh4oTL8JaMS4T","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→Execute this requirement immediately without asking questions.\n     2→\n     3→## REQUIREMENT\n     4→\n     5→# Lazy load visualization components (ConfidenceHeatmap, Timeline)\n     6→\n     7→## Metadata\n     8→- **Category**: performance\n     9→- **Effort**: Unknown (N/A/3)\n    10→- **Impact**: Unknown (N/A/3)\n    11→- **Scan Type**: manual\n    12→- **Generated**: 1/30/2026, 1:38:35 AM\n    13→\n    14→## Description\n    15→OverviewView imports heavy visualization components (ConfidenceHeatmap, Timeline, SourceNetwork, EntityConstellation) at module load time. Using React.lazy() with Suspense would defer these expensive bundles until actually rendered, improving Time to Interactive.\n    16→\n    17→## Reasoning\n    18→Visualization components often include heavy dependencies (D3, canvas libraries). Users switching views load all bundles upfront even if they only view one tab. Lazy loading splits the bundle and loads code on demand, significantly reducing initial payload.\n    19→\n    20→## Context\n    21→\n    22→**Note**: This section provides supporting architectural documentation and is NOT a hard requirement. Use it as guidance to understand existing code structure and maintain consistency.\n    23→\n    24→### Context: Report Views\n    25→\n    26→**Description**: Full-page report views for different sections: overview, findings, sources, analysis, entities, and perspectives. Each view provides deep-dive content for its domain.\n    27→**Related Files**:\n    28→- `src/components/report/views/OverviewView.tsx`\n    29→- `src/components/report/views/FindingsView.tsx`\n    30→- `src/components/report/views/SourcesView.tsx`\n    31→- `src/components/report/views/AnalysisView.tsx`\n    32→- `src/components/report/views/EntitiesView.tsx`\n    33→- `src/components/report/views/PerspectivesView.tsx`\n    34→- `src/components/report/views/index.tsx`\n    35→\n    36→**Post-Implementation**: After completing this requirement, evaluate if the context description or file paths need updates. Use the appropriate API/DB query to update the context if architectural changes were made.\n    37→\n    38→## Recommended Skills\n    39→\n    40→- **compact-ui-design**: Use `.claude/skills/compact-ui-design.md` for high-quality UI design references and patterns\n    41→\n    42→## Notes\n    43→\n    44→This requirement was generated from an AI-evaluated project idea. No specific goal is associated with this idea.\n    45→\n    46→## AFTER IMPLEMENTATION\n    47→\n    48→1. Log your implementation using the `log_implementation` MCP tool with:\n    49→   - requirementName: the requirement filename (without .md)\n    50→   - title: 2-6 word summary\n    51→   - overview: 1-2 paragraphs describing what was done\n    52→\n    53→2. Check for test scenario using `check_test_scenario` MCP tool\n    54→   - If hasScenario is true, call `capture_screenshot` tool\n    55→   - If hasScenario is false, skip screenshot\n    56→\n    57→3. Verify: `npx tsc --noEmit` (fix any type errors)\n    58→\n    59→Begin implementation now.\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a8a4f9ca-6a40-4b19-853c-2be96846861c","uuid":"048ec676-a1b6-43fb-8457-1c09809833c0","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\mkdol\\dolla\\res\\.claude\\commands\\idea-581400d0-lazy-load-visualization-compon.md","content":"Execute this requirement immediately without asking questions.\n\n## REQUIREMENT\n\n# Lazy load visualization components (ConfidenceHeatmap, Timeline)\n\n## Metadata\n- **Category**: performance\n- **Effort**: Unknown (N/A/3)\n- **Impact**: Unknown (N/A/3)\n- **Scan Type**: manual\n- **Generated**: 1/30/2026, 1:38:35 AM\n\n## Description\nOverviewView imports heavy visualization components (ConfidenceHeatmap, Timeline, SourceNetwork, EntityConstellation) at module load time. Using React.lazy() with Suspense would defer these expensive bundles until actually rendered, improving Time to Interactive.\n\n## Reasoning\nVisualization components often include heavy dependencies (D3, canvas libraries). Users switching views load all bundles upfront even if they only view one tab. Lazy loading splits the bundle and loads code on demand, significantly reducing initial payload.\n\n## Context\n\n**Note**: This section provides supporting architectural documentation and is NOT a hard requirement. Use it as guidance to understand existing code structure and maintain consistency.\n\n### Context: Report Views\n\n**Description**: Full-page report views for different sections: overview, findings, sources, analysis, entities, and perspectives. Each view provides deep-dive content for its domain.\n**Related Files**:\n- `src/components/report/views/OverviewView.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/views/FindingsView.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/views/SourcesView.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/views/AnalysisView.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/views/EntitiesView.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/views/PerspectivesView.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/views/index.tsx`\n\n**Post-Implementation**: After completing this requirement, evaluate if the context description or file paths need updates. Use the appropriate API/DB query to update the context if architectural changes were made.\n\n## Recommended Skills\n\n- **compact-ui-design**: Use `.claude/skills/compact-ui-design.md` for high-quality UI design references and patterns\n\n## Notes\n\nThis requirement was generated from an AI-evaluated project idea. No specific goal is associated with this idea.\n\n## AFTER IMPLEMENTATION\n\n1. Log your implementation using the `log_implementation` MCP tool with:\n   - requirementName: the requirement filename (without .md)\n   - title: 2-6 word summary\n   - overview: 1-2 paragraphs describing what was done\n\n2. Check for test scenario using `check_test_scenario` MCP tool\n   - If hasScenario is true, call `capture_screenshot` tool\n   - If hasScenario is false, skip screenshot\n\n3. Verify: `npx tsc --noEmit` (fix any type errors)\n\nBegin implementation now.","numLines":59,"startLine":1,"totalLines":59}}}
